  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bfa36fdea331abe4cb2b293833ff63a0, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 188400156672
    m_Localized: "Alter-Echo production has been retired. Gather resources on adventures or harvest planted crops."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 478381752320
    m_Localized: 'Buffs are short-term, timed powers that expire when they run out
      or if you return to town.  They can be autocast after completing the required
      quest for the slot and the autocasting defaults to on. You can toggle it off
      by clicking the slot in the buffs management window.


      Buff cooldowns
      can be reduced via Eva''s Cauldron.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 492340396032
    m_Localized: "Caleb will enter combat automatically, and only engage enemies
      who get in the way! Tasks first fun later.\n\nD' = D \xD7 (1 - A / (A + N))\n\nD
      = incoming damage\nA = defense value (clamped to 0 or higher)\nN = constant
      scalar that controls diminishing returns (default = 25)\nD' = final damage
      taken\n\nReaching your 10th, 100th, 1,000th, and 10,000th kill against a specific
      enemy will grant you 25% bonus damage against that specific enemy.\nReaching
      your 25,000th, and 100,000th kill against a specific enemy will grant you 50%
      bonus damage against that specific enemy."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 512217202688
    m_Localized: "Echoes are alternate versions of Caleb who will shift slightly
      into his reality to help out under various circumstances.\n\nEach echo can
      have a combination of Caleb's skillset. But most Echoes won't have them all.\n\nThe
      main difference in Echo behaviour comes from whether or not they are combat
      enabled.\nCombat-enabled Echoes have two different styles depending on whether
      or not they can also complete tasks. \n\nA combat-enabled Echo that does NOT
      have the ability to do tasks will seek out enemies specifically.\nA combat-enabled
      Echo that DOES have the ability to do tasks will prioritize tasks over combat
      and only engage enemies that see them.\n\nEchoes that do not have combat will
      not be targeted by or target enemies.\n\nDev Note | Right now there are no
      echoes in the game that can do both combat and tasks. Echoes from Milestones
      specifically seek out tasks for that skills milestone EG an echo spawned with
      woodcutting will only seek out woodcutting tasks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 532437942272
    m_Localized: 'For each kill you get on a run, your resource bonus goes up by
      2%. During combat, this is temporarily set to 0%


      Aim to retreat just
      before combat gets too tough for you to handle so that you get as many bonus
      resources as possible!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 698595295232
    m_Localized: 'Tasks are the primary purpose of Caleb''s journey. Gathering resources
      for the town is essential to growth.


      These are completed automatically,
      and you will complete them faster as your skills level.


      Task spawns
      have a range from minimum to maximum distance, however after reaching maximum
      distance their chance to spawn goes down by 90%. With this considered once
      all tasks are at their maximum the weight system will average out and all tasks
      will be equally available based on their weights.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 505754247643136
    m_Localized: 'Quests have different types of conditions that need to be met before
      you hand them in.


      <b>Information</b> | These quests are instantly completed,
      either for story, or to guide you through the intro.

      <b>Gathering</b>
      | These quests require you to gather resources and hand them in to complete.

      <b>Kills</b>
      | Kill enemies and report back to complete these.

      <b>Meet</b> | Require
      you to meet a certain NPC most of whom are found at specific distances reached.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3785742338113536
    m_Localized: "Upon reaching certain distances from the town Carl will reap your
      soul ensuring you don't stray too far. \nYou can view your maximum reaping
      distance in the statistics under the General Tab.\n\nReaping distance is increased
      via the following methods.\n<b>Being Reaped</b> | Increases distance by 1%
      of your current maximum reaping distance. (Except on farmlands)\n<b>Quests</b>
      | Some quests will provide a reaping distance increase."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6939642239008768
    m_Localized: v1.4.3
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7986628786536448
    m_Localized: 'Dragon slaying pope

      tanty.

      Mellifas

      Latimer
      Cross

      MatHeadGetz

      appleguy

      AwesomePhoenix

      boiledpotato

      eli

      GLUTTONY

      Gudu

      Mentocado

      Nuclearion

      Quackers

      Rugmuk

      SaintPlays

      SCHMUGGLER

      WaringMcMarrin'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133160779776
    m_Localized: "Ivan's forge is a magical place. Whether you're chilling in town
      or out on the road, you can help guide him as he improves his smithing skills.\n\nYou
      have access to two toggles while forging:\n\n<b>Stop for Vastium:</b> Always
      stops if you roll a Vastium piece, even if it is a downgrade.\n\n<b>Stat Matching:</b>
      With this enabled, the forge will continue to work until an upgrade has the
      exact same stat types as your equipped piece of gear.\n\nQuality is represented
      by this icon: <sprite=206>\n\nThis is where you craft gear and choose the best
      stats for your build. \nRight now there are 8 stats that can be rolled on gear
      with each piece guaranteeing a specific one.\n\n<sprite=198> = Damage.\n<sprite=200>
      = Attack Speed.\n<sprite=199> = Crit Chance.\n<sprite=205> = Crit Damage. 
      \n\n<sprite=202> = Health.\n<sprite=203> = Regen.\n<sprite=201> = Defense.\n<sprite=204>
      = Movement.\n\n<sprite=192> = Upgrade.\n<sprite=193> = Downgrade. \n<sprite=194>
      = No change.\n<sprite=195> Stat is not on new item.\n<sprite=196> Stat is not
      on old item.\n\n<b>Weapon</b> | Guarantees <sprite=198>\n<b>Helmet</b> | Guarantees
      <sprite=202>\n<b>Chest</b> | Guarantees <sprite=201>\n<b>Boots</b> | Guarantees
      <sprite=204> which is exclusive to this slot.\n\nGear is automatically salvaged
      when you craft a new piece, select a different slot, or close the game.\n\nDepending
      on rarity you can receive up to 5 stats on a piece of gear. There are plans
      to add additional stats to gear in the future!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133185945600
    m_Localized: "Hey guys Dev here. \n\nIf you want your names in the enemy name
      random pool of names then please jump into discord and ask in the EoV Chat
      :)\n\n\u2022 I am considering moving task unlocks to the milestone system.
      Quests would then provide skill xp instead of task unlocks! Let me know your
      thoughts."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9898115700506624
    m_Localized: "<b>Changes</b>\n\u2022 Added two new quests. For the Jam! & Gilliver's
      Travels.\n\u2022 Improved intro message.\n\u2022 Fixed level up alerts showing
      lower values than you had.\n\u2022 Removed the Forge stats Quality Equipped
      block.\n\u2022 Pinned quests now say \"Ready to turn in\" rather than \"Complete.\n\u2022
      Added an overlay when loading a map.\n\u2022 Added a new Mix All Button.\n<b>Backend</b>\n\u2022
      Updated A* to a newer version."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12027031164698624
    m_Localized: "The Cauldron converts selected food into stew. You choose how much to mix; stew gained depends on the food's authored value and the quantity. Taste stew to receive cards using Eva's displayed reward weights.\n\nResource cards improve genuine gathering, enemy drops and town crop harvests for the matching resource. Their copy thresholds are 1, 25, 75, 200, 750, 1500, 3500 and 10000; yield bonuses are 1%, 2%, 3%, 5%, 7%, 10%, 15% and 20%.\n\nA resource category uses the lowest card tier among its unlocked resources. Unowned cards count as tier zero. Category tiers 1 through 8 add 2%, 5%, 10%, 15%, 20%, 30%, 40% and 50% yield to that category. Card and category bonuses add together, up to 70%. Rewards, seeds, refunds and conversions do not receive these bonuses.\n\nThese card tiers are separate from resource rarity. Existing buff-card cooldown and power benefits remain unchanged. Complete all available resource and buff collections to unlock Eternal Boons."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18915029441462272
    m_Localized: 'Items have a low chance of tiering up each time you collect them.
      Town farm harvests do not roll resource tier upgrades.

      Each tier
      above the first grants you bonus resources each time you collect it in the
      future.


      I''m a bit loathe to share this information with you but here
      you go - Orin...


      Tier | Bonus | Chance

      <b>Tier 1</b>
      - 0%\tBase

      <b>Tier 2</b> - 10%\t1 /1,000

      <b>Tier 3</b> - 20%\t1
      / 5,000

      <b>Tier 4</b> - 30%\t1 / 10,000

      <b>Tier 5</b> - 50%\t1
      / 50,000

      <b>Tier 6</b> - 75%\t1 / 100,000

      <b>Tier 7</b> -
      100%\t1 / 250,000

      <b>Tier 8</b> - 150%\t1 / 1,000,000'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25772880722018304
    m_Localized: English (en)
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
